cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its accompanying paper, please cite it as below."
title: "Institutional Representation ABM: Parliamentary, Presidential, and Semi-Presidential Legislative Passage"
abstract: >-
  An agent-based model comparing four democratic legislative institutions —
  pure parliamentary, pure republican/presidential, premier-presidential
  (France), and president-parliamentary (Russia) — on their ability to pass
  legislation, represent constituencies, and remain operational under
  party-system fragmentation and ideological polarisation. Full statistical
  harness with bootstrap confidence intervals, Morris and Sobol sensitivity
  analyses, and mechanism ablations.
authors:
